[gd_scene format=3]

; The Coldstacks, west of the Choir (map offset (204.5, -69)): the frozen layer's hub, the cold archive's
; endless racks, stacked in stone galleries up to the roof. A pilgrim shrine on the floor. Its ways:
;   east, the Choir (back toward the Brink's fall);
;   up the galleries to a hatch in the roof, the Counterweight: an old lift that only rises, to the Undercroft
;     (sealed: not built yet);
;   the Calving, a high doorway on the west wall: up the metal buttress by grip, or by two rings (sealed);
;   down the well and east along the corridor under the floor, the Mere (sealed);
;   the Vault under the corridor, its way plugged with ice (Drill; sealed);
;   the Chimney, a vent in the floor capped with slag (Heat plating; sealed).
; The MapGoal of the built map is here (the end of what is built).

